      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12598210961408
    m_Localized: ' '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 26783519055872
    m_Localized: "G\xFCnther von Schwarzburg's tomb"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27028156030976
    m_Localized: "G\xFCnther von Schwarzburg was a count from Thuringia who was elected
      King of the Romans in 1349. His reign, however, was quite short, as he lost
      the power struggle against Charles IV. He sought refuge in Frankfurt am Main,
      but fell gravely ill there. He eventually abdicated voluntarily. A few weeks
      later, he died and was buried in St. Bartholomew's Church. His fate illustrates
      how quickly power and glory can vanish \u2013 but also that true greatness
      lies in preserving dignity and peace in difficult times."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27919642763264
    m_Localized: "Even before 1967, the church workshops in Erfurt produced artistic
      brass works. A well-known story from the Bible is that of Saul: On the road
      to Damascus, he encountered a bright, heavenly light. This experience completely
      changed his life \u2013 the persecutor Saul became Paul, one of the most important
      apostles. His example shows how profoundly faith can transform a person. To
      this day, his letters and thoughts shape Christianity. His transformation is
      a powerful symbol of hope and new beginnings."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27877267709952
    m_Localized: Saul before Damascus
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28304239468544
    m_Localized: The high altar, dedicated to the Evangelist John, is located on
      the east side of the high choir. The lower part, a stone block with blind arcades,
      dates from the time the choir was built (1280). A three-wing carved altar,
      originally from Paul's Church, has adorned this square since the 16th century.
      The masterpiece by Linhart Koenberg, an outstanding Erfurt master carver of
      the 15th century, is dated 1492. The apostles Paul and Peter are painted on
      the outside. The second side of the wings shows various scenes, particularly
      during Lent.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28271582617600
    m_Localized: The High altar
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30219836825600
    m_Localized: "Master Eckhart was a well-known German theologian and mystic. He
      conceived the idea of \u200B\u200Ba \"prayer church.\" By this, he meant that
      prayer is more than just a fixed ritual. It is something very personal and
      can transform a person. According to Eckhart, every person can connect with
      God through honest reflection and silent prayer. This brings inner peace and
      a sense of fulfillment. The \"prayer church\" invites people to seek God's
      closeness within themselves. In this way, they can feel the power of prayer
      in their everyday lives and experience how it transforms their lives."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28701037404160
    m_Localized: Master Eckhart and the Prayers' Church
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30745177595904
    m_Localized: Gustav Adolf Chandelier
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 30611521904640
    m_Localized: 'In the high choir hangs a large candlestick, the "Gustav Adolf
      Candlestick," featuring eight figures of the apostles. Eduard Bode donated
      it to the Preachers'' Church in 1647. He wanted to honor the Swedish King Gustav
      II Adolf with this donation. At the same time, he also had personal reasons:
      Bode had no children and was said to have had a relationship with Maria Krondorferin.
      At the time, many people derogatorily called her a "poor whore." The candlestick
      therefore combines personal feelings of guilt with the desire to demonstrate
      faith. Today, it is considered a symbol of repentance, remembrance, and the
      hope of forgiveness from God.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31042344034304
    m_Localized: Aurifaber's tomb
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31081011322880
    m_Localized: "Johannes Aurifaber, also known as Johann Goldschmidt, was an important
      reformer in the 16th century. He studied in Wittenberg and met Martin Luther
      there personally. Luther's ideas had a profound influence on him. Aurifaber
      helped spread the new ideas of the Reformation\u2014for example, through translations
      and sermons. With his work, he had a profound impact on the religious development
      of his time."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31300247592960
    m_Localized: Madonna
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 31328294903808
    m_Localized: 'The sculpture of the Virgin Mary is also called the "Schmedestedt
      Madonna." Along with a Crucifixion panel, it was part of the original furnishings
      of the choir screen. A choir screen is a decorative wall or grille that separates
      the choir from the rest of the church. What is particularly striking about
      the Madonna is its shape: her body is slender and depicted in an elegant S-line.
      Above, the tight clothing emphasizes her body shape. Below, however, one can
      see many long folds in the fabric. They hang straight down and almost completely
      cover her legs.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1150275190759424
    m_Localized: "<b>Teachers who supervised our project:</b>\r\n\r\nIn the early
      development phase:\r\n<i>Dr. Blasius</i>\r\n\r\nIn the late development phase:\r\n<i>Mr.
      Quent</i>\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Our development team:</b>\r\n\r\n<b>Adrian E.</b>\r\nProgramming,
      3D scanning, research, organization, reference images, playtesting\r\n\r\n<b>Dmytro
      A.</b>\r\nModeling, playtesting, reference images, organization\r\n\r\n<b>Gabriel
      R.</b>\r\nResearch, test coordination, reference images, playtesting\r\n\r\n<b>Alex
      L.</b>\r\nReference images, organization, research\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Assets & Resources:</b>\r\n\r\n<b>Skybox</b>\r\nPolyhaven\r\n\r\n<b>Player
      model (modified)</b>\r\nMaxime66410\r\n\r\n<b>Footstep sounds</b>\r\nFesliyan
      Studio\r\n\r\n<b>Background music</b>\r\nFesliyan Studio\r\n\r\n<b>Sandstone
      textures</b>\r\nPolyhaven\r\n\r\n<b>Other textures</b>\r\nAmbientCG, Polyhaven\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Special
      thanks to:</b>\r\n<i>Pastor Ackermann</i>\r\nfor recording his voice for the
      project\r\n\r\nPlaytesters\r\nfor valuable feedback and suggestions for improvement\r\n\r\n\xA9
      2025 Crisis Portabe\r\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
